{
  "id": "PPA-02",
  "title": "Photosynthesis & Chloroplast Bioenergetics",
  "subtitle": "Z-scheme photochemistry, thylakoid electron transport, cyclic electron flow, and photophosphorylation",
  "caption": "Photosynthetic light reactions and thylakoid bioenergetics redrawn with deterministic geometry. Captures linear electron flow from water splitting at photosystem II (PSII) through the plastoquinone pool, cytochrome b6f complex, and plastocyanin to photosystem I (PSI), with ferredoxin-NADP+ reductase (FNR) producing NADPH. Cyclic electron flow via PGR5/PGRL1 and the chloroplast ATP synthase CF0-CF1 complex are explicitly resolved.",
  "species_anchor": "arabidopsis_thaliana",
